      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T22:11:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(setup)!: one WCS per setup; G54-G59 is only the setup's post label\n\nA setup now owns exactly one work coordinate system: SetupDef.wcs names\none entity (was a six-slot list) and SetupDef.work_offset is only the\nword the post writes for it - relabelling moves no origin and no height.\nThe browser shows one row, plain \"WCS\" (its word as the faint suffix),\nnever G54..G59 slot rows; it targets the WCS page, which edits the\nactive setup's origin through the undoable SetWcs. SetWcsOrigin::new\ntakes no slot; UiTarget::WcsSlot(i) became UiTarget::Wcs. The setup\nsheet, WCS page, rotation refusal, MCP get_job and height chips speak\nof \"WCS (G55)\" / \"WCS G55\".\n\nProject v54 (project::wcs_one): each v53 setup keeps the entity (name\nand placement) of the slot it posted, so single-WCS documents post byte\nfor byte; placed slots no setup posted are dropped with a load note\n(project::open_noted / load_noted, shown in the status line); a\nno-setup document keeps G54; an operation in a setup the file lacks\nkeeps its zero (<setup>/G54 -> <setup>/WCS). Two origins inside one\nsetup only arise from v51-or-older files, which the v52 rung already\nrefuses by name. The two-setups-same-word refusal stands.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: project files are v54 (\"wcs\" is one name, unreadable\nby older builds); placed work-offset slots no setup posted are dropped\non load (with a note); SetWcsOrigin::new lost its slot argument.\n\nFixes #342\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
