      "message": "Merge origin/main into issue/342-one-wcs (#327 non-finite WCS, #257 comments, #298)\n\nConflicts and how they were kept:\n- crates/app/src/commands/set_wcs.rs: the one-WCS signature\n  SetWcsOrigin::new(world, location) of #342 plus #332's non-finite /\n  zero-norm validation; its refusals now name the active setup's WCS by\n  its label (\"WCS (G55): rotation must be finite ...\") instead of a slot.\n- crates/app/src/setup_sheet/sections.rs: #342's single \"WCS (G5x)\" line\n  and program offset via the setup, plus #332's rotation / non-finite\n  line under it.\n\nSemantic ports (not flagged by git):\n- tests/rotated_wcs.rs: #332's SetWcsOrigin test placed a G55 slot; it\n  now labels Setup1 G55 and places its one WCS, asserting \"WCS (G55)\";\n  the post-gate assertions read \"the WCS (G54) has a non-finite\n  placement\", the wording the one-WCS gate writes.\n- project/validate.rs: the load refusal says \"WCS '<name>'\" (plain label).\n- tests/one_wcs.rs: new pin that #332's load check still runs on the\n  v53 -> v54 rung's posted slot (zero-norm rotation refused by name).\n- docs/decisions/327: wording updated to the one-WCS law.\n\nRefs #342\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
